<!-- ehos_app:web -->
# The web layer

`lib/<%= @app %>_web/` is how people and other applications reach this one: the router, the
controllers, the components and layouts, and the health plug EHOS probes.

This section is the installer's (`ehos_app`), between its two markers: an upgrade of the template
rewrites it. Write this application's own rules below it.

- **Commands reach a contract only through `EhOsContract.Plug`**, in a router pipeline that starts
  with `EhOsContract.Auth.Plug`. Never route to a command around it.
- **A page that needs a person** sits behind the `:signed_in` pipeline, and reads them with
  `EhOsContract.Auth.Session.actor/1`. People sign in through EHOS at `/auth/ehos`, never through
  a login of this application's own. Keep EHOS's tokens out of assigns and pages: a credential for
  another application (`Session.credential/3`) is sent from the server.<%= if @access_page do %>
  `AccessController`, which the template routed at `/access`, is such a page.<% end %>
- **The way in and out is at the top of the root layout**, `components/layouts/root.html.heex`:
  `SignInComponents.sign_in_or_out/1`, which reads the session from `@conn`. Every page renders
  the root layout, a LiveView's included, so replacing the home page keeps it. Keep it there, or
  in another template that has a conn: a LiveView's own layout has none.
- **The health plug** serves `/health/live` and `/health/ready` on the health port `ehos.yaml`
  declares. EHOS probes it there, and never exposes that port.
<%= if @phoenix_rules do %>- **Phoenix's rules** for the version this project was generated with are in
  [docs/phoenix.md](../../docs/phoenix.md). Read them before changing a template, a component, a
  LiveView or a route.
<% end %><%= if @design_system_declined do %>- **The UI's look is this application's own**: it declined the EmpoweredHouse design system,
  and `assets/css/app.css` says so above where its import was. Build on `core_components.ex` and
  this application's own styles.
<% else %>- **The UI follows the EmpoweredHouse design system** by default, from the `ehos_design`
  dependency: `assets/css/app.css` <%= if @design_system_imported, do: "imports it", else: "is to import it ([ARCHITECTURE.md](../../ARCHITECTURE.md))" %>, and the endpoint serves its fonts. Build on
  `core_components.ex`, which it styles, and on its utilities (`bg-surface-1`,
  `text-fg-secondary`, `border-line-faint`) rather than Tailwind's own colours. Override a token
  at the end of `app.css`; `<%= @design_system %>/README.md` says how to replace the look.
<% end %>
<!-- /ehos_app:web -->
